<title>UK: BAe, Rolls seek end to ownership limit.</title>
<headline>BAe, Rolls seek end to ownership limit.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Aerospace Plc and Rolls Royce Plc have urged the British government to scrap the 29.5 percent limit on foreign shareholdings imposed when the two groups were privatised in the 1980s, the companies said.</p>
<p>&quot;The government has set a limit on the number of foreign-owned shares in British Aerospace and Rolls Royce. In an international market these days it would be advantageous if we didn't have such a situation,&quot; said Mike Peters, communications executive at BAe.</p>
<p>&quot;Both Rolls Royce and British Aerospace have had discussions with the government about the situation,&quot; he told Reuters.</p>
<p>((-- London Newsroom +44-171-542-7717))</p>
